orow(32, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL LOVE THE LORD YOUR GOD" (6:5) — ACT FROM LOVE. SCRIPTURE DISTINGUISHES ONE WHO ACTS FROM LOVE FROM ONE WHO ACTS FROM FEAR: THE ONE WHO ACTS FROM LOVE, HIS REWARD IS DOUBLED AND REDOUBLED; FOR IT SAYS "THE LORD YOUR GOD YOU SHALL FEAR AND HIM YOU SHALL SERVE" (10:20) — THERE IS A MAN WHO FEARS HIS FELLOW, AND WHEN THE FELLOW NEEDS HIM HE LEAVES HIM AND GOES; BUT YOU — ACT FROM LOVE, FOR THERE IS NO LOVE WHERE THERE IS FEAR NOR FEAR WHERE THERE IS LOVE, SAVE IN THE MEASURE OF THE ALL-PRESENT ALONE. The row on 6:5 ({SP_(32, 1, "עשה", "מאהבה")} "act from love"; {SP_(32, 1, "הפריש", "בין", "העושה", "מאהבה", "לעושה", "מיראה")} "Scripture distinguishes the one who acts from love from the one who acts from fear"; {SP_(32, 1, "שכרו", "כפול", "ומכפל")} "his reward is doubled and redoubled"; {SP_(32, 1, "אלא", "במדת", "מקום", "בלבד")} "save in the measure of the All-Present alone"): 10:20 READ AS THE FEARER\'S SEAT — the four clauses "fear, serve, cleave, swear" quoted for their first two against 6:5\'s "love"; the chapter\'s own 10:12 puts fear and love in one demand, which the row resolves in God alone. Read before at sitting 4 (the Shema\'s piska on 6:5), REREAD WHOLE here; the translator\'s footnote on the last clause noted, no interpolation (NO MIDDAH CODE — the row argues by a distinction between two verses, its own words on its bytes; the fear/love pair of 10:12 and 10:20 the compile\'s cell by CALL to 6:13).')
orow(301, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HE WENT DOWN TO EGYPT" (26:5) — IT TEACHES THAT HE DID NOT GO DOWN TO SETTLE BUT TO SOJOURN THERE. LEST YOU SAY HE WENT DOWN TO TAKE THE ROYAL CROWN, THE TEACHING SAYS "AND HE SOJOURNED THERE". COULD IT BE WITH MANY MULTITUDES? THE TEACHING SAYS "WITH FEW" — AS IT IS SAID "WITH SEVENTY PERSONS YOUR FATHERS WENT DOWN TO EGYPT" (10:22). The row on 26:5 ({SP_(301, 4, "להשתקע", "אלא", "לגור", "שם")} "not to settle but to sojourn there"; {SP_(301, 4, "כתר", "מלכות")} "the royal crown"; {SP_(301, 4, "במתי", "מעט")} "with few"; {SP_(301, 4, "בשבעים", "נפש", "ירדו", "אבותיך", "מצרימה")} "with seventy persons your fathers went down to Egypt" — QUOTED PLENE, "your fathers" with the vav the DB does not write at 10:22 (asserted on the bytes)): the first-fruits confession\'s "few" measured by this chapter\'s seventy — the verse the shelf\'s number for "few". Fresh; the English translator\'s note that the passage is poorly attested in copies of the Sifrei and absent from the Haggadah recorded, the row kept whole in both files (NO MIDDAH CODE — a proof-text read for its count; the seventy the Joseph runner\'s cell by CALL at the compile).')
orow(311, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "WHEN THE MOST HIGH GAVE THE NATIONS THEIR INHERITANCE" (32:8) — WHEN THE HOLY ONE GAVE THE NATIONS THEIR INHERITANCE FROM AMONG THE FEARERS OF SIN AND THE WORTHY AMONG THEM; "WHEN HE SEPARATED THE SONS OF ADAM" — THIS IS THE GENERATION OF THE DISPERSION, AS IT IS SAID "AND FROM THERE THE LORD SCATTERED THEM" (GENESIS 11:9); "HE SET THE BORDERS OF THE PEOPLES" — R. ELIEZER THE SON OF R. YOSE THE GALILEAN SAYS: IT SAYS "SIXTY ARE THE QUEENS AND EIGHTY THE CONCUBINES" (SONG OF SONGS 6:8) — SIXTY AND EIGHTY ARE A HUNDRED AND FORTY; OUR FATHERS WENT DOWN TO EGYPT WITH ONLY SEVENTY SOULS, AS IT IS SAID "WITH SEVENTY SOULS YOUR FATHERS WENT DOWN" (10:22) — AND SO IT SAYS "THE BORDERS OF THE PEOPLES": NOT "THE BORDER OF THE PEOPLES" IS WRITTEN HERE BUT "THE BORDERS" — THE NATIONS MERITED TO TAKE TWO SHARES BY THE NUMBER OF THE CHILDREN OF ISRAEL. The row on 32:8 ({SP_(311, 5, "זה", "דור", "הפלגה")} "this is the generation of the dispersion"; {SP_(311, 5, "ששים", "ושמנים", "הרי", "מאה", "וארבעים")} "sixty and eighty are a hundred and forty"; {SP_(311, 5, "בשבעים", "נפש", "ירדו", "אבתיך")} "with seventy souls your fathers went down" — QUOTED DEFECTIVE, as the DB writes it; {SP_(311, 5, "גבולי", "עמים", "אין", "כתוב", "כאן", "אלא", "גבלת", "עמים")} "not the border of the peoples is written here but the borders of the peoples"; {SP_(311, 5, "שני", "חלקים")} "two shares"): THE ARITHMETIC OF THE NATIONS AGAINST THE SEVENTY — a hundred and forty nations to seventy souls, reconciled by reading the plural "borders" as two shares each; the two Sifrei rows quote 10:22 with two spellings of "your fathers". Read before at the Babel sitting (on 11:9) and credited at the separation sitting, REREAD WHOLE here (E10 — the repeated expression signifies: "borders", not "border", read for its number, as chapter 6\'s 31:8 and 31:10 were, checked in MIDDOT.md before it was typed; the count read from the ink).')

